{"rank":2,"title":"The headline is the weakest text on the page and the reason to book here is buried","target":"the headline is the largest and darkest text on the page, with a real step up from the lead, in the body color, and carries the book-direct, no-fee point","fix_direction":"Make the headline clearly the largest and darkest thing on the page, with a real step up from the lead. Put the book-direct, no-fee point in it or right under it, and darken the h1 to the body color. A week's hire price or the agency fee the visitor avoids would help, but that figure must come from the maker; the maker must supply it.","sel":"h1"}
{"rank":3,"title":"Two buttons do one job, and the wrong one is primary","target":"\"Search\" is the one filled primary button; the hero button is removed or has a clearly different job","fix_direction":"Make \"Search\" the one filled primary button. Remove the hero button, or give it a clearly different job.","sel":"button"}
{"rank":4,"title":"A holiday on the water with nothing to look at","target":"one specific image of this company's boats or routes fills the empty area under the button without pushing the form down","fix_direction":"Add one specific image of this company's boats or routes, not a stock scene, placed so it fills the empty area under the button rather than pushing the form down. The maker must supply the image.","sel":null}
{"rank":5,"title":"On wide screens the page splits in two, with empty space between","target":"content held in one width cap so the form stays near the text, with the routes pulled into the empty space or placed where the link to the Base field is visible","fix_direction":"Keep the content in one width cap so the form stays near the text. Pull the routes up into the empty space, or place them where the connection to the Base field is visible.","sel":null}
{"rank":null,"title":"The h1 and the gray route figures are just under 4.5:1 contrast","target":"contrast of at least 4.5:1","fix_direction":"Darken the gray one step.","sel":"h1"}
{"rank":null,"title":"On the phone the route figures split numbers from their units and the route names wrap","target":"each figure on one line","fix_direction":"Keep each figure on one line, which the one-column layout should give it room for.","sel":"ul > li:nth-of-type(2) > span:nth-of-type(2)"}
{"rank":null,"title":"On the tablet the lead runs in a narrow column and ends with a single word","target":"a wider text column, or the form stacked under the text, with no single word on the last line","fix_direction":"Give the text column more width, or stack the form under it.","sel":"p.lead"}
{"rank":null,"title":"The select and input borders look pale and may be below 3:1","target":"border contrast of at least 3:1 against the white card","fix_direction":"Measure the border color and darken it if it fails.","sel":"form.search > label:nth-of-type(1) > select"}
{"rank":null,"title":"The start date field shows no year and looks like a plain text field","target":"the year is shown, or it is clear that a date picker sets the value","fix_direction":"Show the year, or make it clear that a date picker sets the value.","sel":"input"}

